# One name per path, applied to THIS MACHINE's /usr -- updatebuild reads
# this and performs each line, once, idempotently.  The names are the
# repository checkout's, so the tree here, the checkout, and taripnx's archive
# all agree, and the archive extracts onto a case-insensitive filesystem
# without a collision.  build/casenames carries the evidence per decision;
# the two schemes are one scheme.
#
# u_u_ MARKS A DOUBLE COLLISION: ideal/lib held ARC, Arc and arc, and the
# extractor's u_ARC and u_Arc collide with each other on the Mac -- the
# checkout silently LOST Arc's 830 bytes (and charlib's lH, four times) until
# this machine's tree gave them back.  v10tapes/CASEMAP records the extractor
# intending both names; only one survived.
#
# rm is confined to: files the build regenerates (USERMEM, three Version.c),
# the sail hard-link's second name, an unreferenced header (libstring
# string.h), guest-local debris on no tape (efl/Efix, efl/efix, odist/notes),
# and two tape binaries whose names collide with their own build products
# (Pret, Trace -- recoverable from the tapes).
#
